{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "025X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0002": "$h_T$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-scheme-is-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:13ad1b5df5ff67115e84136338c3e314ca8b2ee675a232bb55731a6f5102e5ec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b9aafd2d2d0850d6318441135bde8c8eb344336446ee4a71f585f931edccaa58", "source_text": "A scheme is an algebraic space. More precisely,\ngiven a scheme <MATH_0001>\nthe representable functor <MATH_0002> is an algebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ba7d7ac3ad6008d9e68e09d9220e58a987ed83f5ecc98fb9d68900703d8f2279", "unit_id": "tag:025Z:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025X", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$h_T$", "MATH_0002": "$h_T \\to h_T \\times h_T = h_{T \\times T}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$h_T \\to h_T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-general}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9a99be206b49298a88fb81ae94f9021af188918d2c9cbdbe5ca5131ea7d5255e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a280ed46dd257b7bb3f4e748ef049cbd4f7ae0c71eee00bdd311d83436c6932e", "source_text": "The functor <MATH_0001> is a sheaf by our remarks in Section <REF_0001>.\nThe diagonal <MATH_0002> is\nrepresentable because <MATH_0003> has fibre products.\nThe identity map <MATH_0004> is surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8e90f4ea1eb7699b0ac8a336c8037d682316943eedcb7f36b7610b18de1d7e87", "unit_id": "tag:025Z:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "025X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$F'$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f : F \\to F'$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$F'$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-morphism-algebraic-spaces}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:25d1176677825a2e5a64fa28b3d24bc4470d24543005d007d092465ddc26710f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:216da579e98886db8d7a87ad876ec8ae795f2ef9c43bfe0a28326b54a0d4d4a7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>morphism <MATH_0004> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a transformation of functors from <MATH_0006> to <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d3309579bf528a169bb16e1e9571b0455c666c1b2c9acfb5698dd4f04b8247a6", "unit_id": "tag:0260:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$T/S \\mapsto h_T$", "MATH_0004": "$T/S$", "MATH_0005": "$f : T \\to F$", "MATH_0006": "$T$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "MATH_0008": "$T \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0009": "$F$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$f : h_T \\to F$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34c3bca5a6fb85f156aa1d2b7590447f46c4630f8adff232b6014e7add76bdab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d0e5f92869dcf65f7998f159d37cb47f71ff9f2671efe3d6f86f866ab03fdae2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe category of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0001> contains the category\n<MATH_0002> as a full subcategory via the\nYoneda embedding <MATH_0003>. From now on we no longer distinguish\nbetween a scheme <MATH_0004> and the algebraic space it represents.\nThus when we say ``Let <MATH_0005> be a morphism from the scheme\n<MATH_0006> to the algebraic space <MATH_0007>'', we mean that\n<MATH_0008>, that <MATH_0009> is an\nalgebraic space over <MATH_0010>, and that <MATH_0011> is a morphism\nof algebraic spaces over <MATH_0012>.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:79d45b8f1f9511b90c6ed89ee7b606dd1356d0123c20e58e370e9c66e8b21ed0", "unit_id": "tag:025X:prose-0003"}
